ECP-1 Payment Management 

Title: Payment Management 

Description: 

Manage payment processing, refunds, transaction validation, and payment gateway integration. 

 

ECP-2 Credit card payment fails during checkout (DONE) 

Description: 

Users receive a 500 Internal Server Error when attempting to complete payment using credit cards. Orders are not generated. 

  

Priority: Highest 

Root Cause: 

Payment token became null when VISA card validation service timed out. 

  

The payment workflow attempted to process the transaction without validating the token and resulted in a 500 Internal Server Error. 

Resolution: 

Added null validation before payment processing. 

  

Implemented retry logic for payment gateway service calls and improved error handling for timeout scenarios. 

  

Verified successfully in QA environment. 

 

ECP-3 Duplicate payment transactions created for single order (DONE) 

Description: 

Certain users report being charged twice after clicking the Pay button only once. 

   

Priority: High 

Root Cause: 

Users clicked the Pay button multiple times while waiting for the response. 

  

Frontend allowed repeated submissions and generated duplicate API requests. 

Resolution: 

Added debounce mechanism on the payment button. 

  

Disabled multiple submissions until payment response is received. 

  

Verified duplicate transactions are no longer created. 

 

ECP-4 Refund request remains in processing state 

Description: 

Refunds initiated by customers never move beyond the processing status. 

  

Priority: High 

ECP-5 Payment succeeds but order is not created 

Description: 

Payment gateway confirms successful payment but no order record is generated.  

Priority: Highest 

ECP-6 Expired debit cards accepted during payment 

Description: 

System allows checkout using expired debit cards. 

  

Priority: Medium 

 

ECP-7 Shopping Cart Management 

Title: Shopping Cart Management 

Description: 

Handle cart operations such as add, update, remove, quantity management, and coupon application. 

ECP-8 Cart quantity not updating (DONE) 

Description: 

Users cannot increase or decrease product quantity in the shopping cart. 

  

Priority: High 

 

Root Cause: 

 

Cart update API was not persisting item quantity changes to the database. 

  

CartService update method failed to invoke repository save operation. 

Resolution: 

Updated CartService quantity update logic. 

  

Added repository persistence call and verified quantity changes are correctly stored. 

ECP-9 Coupon code not applied (DONE) 

Description: 

Valid coupon codes fail to reduce order total. 

  

Priority: High 

Root Cause: 

Coupon validation service incorrectly marked active coupons as expired due to timezone conversion issues. 

Resolution: 

Updated coupon validation logic. 

  

Normalized timezone handling and corrected expiration date comparison logic. 

  

Verified coupon application across all supported regions. 

ECP-10 Cart items disappear after page refresh 

Description: 

Products added to cart are removed after refreshing the browser. 

   

Priority: High 

ECP-11 Cart total calculation incorrect 

Description: 

Displayed cart total does not match product prices. 

  

Priority: High 

ECP-12 Guest user cart not retained 

Description: 

Guest user cart becomes empty after navigating between pages. 

   

Priority: Medium 

ECP-13 Product Catalog Management 

Title: Product Catalog Management 

Description: 

Manage products, search, filters, pricing, reviews, and product information. 

ECP-14 Product search returns no results (DONE) 

Description: 

Valid products are not returned in search results. 

   

Priority: High 

Root Cause: 

Search index was not refreshed after product creation and updates. 

  

Newly created products were missing from the search database. 

Resolution: 

Added automatic reindexing after product updates. 

  

Implemented search index synchronization process. 

  

Verified products appear immediately in search results. 

 

ECP-15 Product image failing to load 

Description: 

Several product images display as broken images. 

  

Priority: Medium 

ECP-16 Product filters not working 

Description: 

Filtering by category, brand, or price produces incorrect results. 

  

Priority: High 

ECP-17 Incorrect product price displayed 

Description: 

Price displayed on product page differs from checkout value. 

 

Priority: High 

 

ECP-18 Product reviews not visible 

Description: 

Customer reviews fail to load for multiple products. 

  

Priority: Medium 

ECP-19 User Authentication & Security 

Title: User Authentication & Security 

Description: 

User registration, login, session management, password reset, and token validation. 

 

ECP-20 User login failing with valid credentials (DONE) 

Description: 

Registered users cannot log in despite providing correct credentials. 

  

Priority: Highest 

Root Cause: 

JWT secret key configuration mismatch existed between authentication service instances. 

  

Token generation and validation used different secrets. 

Resolution: 

Unified JWT configuration across all deployment environments. 

  

Updated authentication service configuration and verified successful login operations. 

ECP-21 Password reset email not received 

Description: 

Reset password requests do not send emails. 

  

Priority: High 

ECP-22 User session expires unexpectedly (DONE) 

Description: 

Users are logged out within a few minutes of authentication. 

  

Priority: High 

Root Cause: 

Session timeout value was incorrectly configured to five minutes due to environment configuration override. 

Resolution: 

Updated session timeout configuration to thirty minutes. 

  

Removed conflicting environment override settings. 

  

Verified session stability across browsers. 

ECP-23 Account registration throws validation error 

Description: 

New users cannot register due to unexpected validation failures. 

  

Priority: High 

ECP-24 JWT token validation failing 

Description: 

Authenticated API requests are rejected with unauthorized errors. 

  

Priority: Highest 

ECP-25 Order Processing 

Title: Order Processing 

Description: 

Order creation, order history, shipping updates, and notification management. 

ECP-26 Order history page is empty (DONE) 

Description: 

Customers cannot view previous orders. 

   

Priority: High 

Root Cause: 

Order repository query returned only active orders and excluded completed or archived orders. 

  

Historical order data was filtered incorrectly. 

Resolution: 

Updated repository query to return complete order history. 

  

Added integration tests to validate order retrieval functionality. 

ECP-27 Order confirmation email not sent 

Description: 

Customers do not receive confirmation emails after order placement. 

  

Priority: Medium 

ECP-28 Order status not updated after shipping 

Description: 

Orders remain in Processing status even after shipment. 

  

Priority: High 

ECP-29 Inventory Management 

Title: Inventory Management 

Description: 

Stock allocation, stock updates, inventory validation, and warehouse synchronization. 

ECP-30 Inventory count not updated after purchase (DONE) 

Description: 

Product stock quantity remains unchanged after successful orders. 

  

Priority: High 

Root Cause: 

Inventory update event was not triggered following successful order creation. 

  

Stock synchronization workflow failed to execute. 

Resolution: 

Added inventory event listener after order confirmation. 

  

Verified inventory is updated immediately after successful purchase. 

 

ECP-31 Negative inventory generated for high-demand products (DONE) 

Description: 

Stock values become negative after multiple simultaneous purchases. 

  

Priority: Highest 

Root Cause: 

Concurrent purchases bypassed stock validation checks. 

  

Multiple transactions updated inventory simultaneously causing race conditions. 

Resolution: 

Implemented inventory locking mechanism. 

  

Added stock validation before order confirmation and prevented negative inventory values. 

  

Verified under load testing. 

 